# BUGS

srvfs keeps its posts in memory: a restart loses them, and svcd lists the `srvmode=` posts only when it first starts srvfs.
There are at most 64 posts, 64 users and 63-byte names.
A post's mode cannot be changed after it is made, and its owner is the attaching user's name, unchecked until keyd (M10).
